//? Title: Occlusion sensitivity:actual finite patches and overlap accounting
//? Requires: vanilla_saliency.mepml
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An image classifier may change its score when a visible region is replaced. Evaluate every actual rectangular replacement on genuine MNIST images,retain signed fixed-category score changes,and show explicit edge coverage and replacement,patch,target and weight controls.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.11_interpretability/occlusion_sensitivity.cpp`.

> The method

For patchR,replacementr and fixed raw score s_c,measure the finite change directly. Project the patch measurements onto pixels by averaging all covering patch drops:

$$ D_R=s_c(x)-s_c(x_{R\leftarrow r}),\qquad M_p=\frac{\sum_{R:p\in R}D_R}{\#\{R:p\in R\}}. $$
\alttext(The signed patch effect is the original fixed-category score minus its actual replacement score;the pixel display averages effects of every patch covering that pixel.)

Coverage is positive everywhere because boundary anchors are explicit and stride never exceeds patch size. No derivative,learned explainer or optimizer replaces the actual frozen-model predictions. The model fitting loop remains explicit in vanilla_saliency.

The concept diagram below is drawn by `dm::graphics::Diagram`. Its editable C++
source is the complete block below; regeneration uses the same datamunge toolchain
as the numerical examples. Exports consume the saved local SVG.

```{cpp, file="figures/occlusion_sensitivity_concept.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram;
  diagram.node("n0", {0.0, 0}, "Actual image\n fixed finite patch");
  diagram.node("n1", {5.2, 0}, "Re-evaluate same\n raw category");
  diagram.node("n2", {10.4, 0}, "Signed score drops\n overlap mean and controls");
  diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
  diagram.save_svg("build/occlusion_sensitivity_concept.svg");
}
