// result_end
\caption(All ten per-case control changes and actual signed primary patch counts. Every raw primary drop and rectangle is saved and printed;overlap-averaged pixels are summaries of finite interventions rather than additive causal contributions.)
\alttext(All ten per-case control changes and actual signed primary patch counts. Every raw primary drop and rectangle is saved and printed;overlap-averaged pixels are summaries of finite interventions rather than additive causal contributions.)


> Conclusion

Original observations,every modified input,all signed score changes and explicit coverage make the experiment reproducible. Identity/full checks and independent finite-patch oracles validate computation;replacement,size,stride,target and model dependence limit any pixelwise or causal interpretation.

> References

- [Zeiler and Fergus(2014),Visualizing and Understanding Convolutional Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.2901).
